WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:01.770
The year is 1985.

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:02.770
16th of February.

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:10.510
A pair of researchers aboard a Model SM-03
deep sea submersible are descending into the

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.180
depths of the Atlantic Ocean.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:17.940
Hours ago, they were somewhere just off the
coast of France, surrounded by blue sky, the

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:21.420
smell of the sea, and the warm embrace of
the sun.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.910
But now, only cold darkness surrounds them.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:30.859
The depth of the ocean so vast and overwhelming
even light could not escape it’s grasp.

00:00:30.859 --> 00:00:37.300
The two-man team are members of MTF Gamma-6,
also known as the DEEP FEEDERS a special task

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:43.790
force that specializes in the investigation
and tracking of deep-sea or oceanic anomalies.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:49.670
Their mission; to locate and investigate the
wreckage of a WW2 German warship known as

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:54.129
the Bismarck, thought by the general public
to have gone down in a naval battle with the

00:00:54.129 --> 00:00:56.480
British in 1941.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.829
But the story the public doesn’t know..
is the real reason the pair of Foundation

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:04.850
members were tasked with locating the ship’s
wreckage site.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:09.249
Unfortunately for these researchers, today
would be remembered for something far worse

00:01:09.249 --> 00:01:11.549
than they had anticipated.

00:01:11.549 --> 00:01:15.850
Radio transmissions recorded by the Gamma-6
duo, detailed the events that took place upon

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:19.270
finding the The Bismarck designated SCP-4217.

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:25.670
The Bismarck lay at the bottom of the ocean
partially submerged in the sea floor, but,

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:31.310
to the astonishment of researchers, it appeared
to be perfectly intact, with no signs of damage

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:33.999
from it’s previous naval engagements.

00:01:33.999 --> 00:01:38.969
Gamma-6 member Charles Miller comments:
“Even after the better part of five decades,

00:01:38.969 --> 00:01:41.380
this ship is still in pristine condition.

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:44.749
There is no water damage anywhere that I can
see.

00:01:44.749 --> 00:01:50.020
Even stranger, no ocean sediment has accumulated
on the hull of the ship whatsoever.”

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:54.939
Prompted to investigate closer, agent Victor
Miller begins operation of the crew’s Model

00:01:54.939 --> 00:02:00.869
RV-1 Marine Probe, an unmanned robotic exploratory
drone that allows the researchers to explore

00:02:00.869 --> 00:02:03.399
the interior of the ship’s wreckage.

00:02:03.399 --> 00:02:05.500
What they found unnerved them.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.000
Or better said, what they didn't find.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:13.379
Just as the outside of the vessel appeared
free of any corrosion or wear, the interior

00:02:13.379 --> 00:02:16.430
of the ship was just as immaculate.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:22.629
The hallways were clean, the walls adorned
freshly printed signs in still legible German.

00:02:22.629 --> 00:02:28.290
Even the Nazi symbols painted onto command
centers still held no sign of disintegration.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:32.239
It was as if the ship had just come off the
assembly line.

00:02:32.239 --> 00:02:35.790
But strangest of all was the lack of skeletal
remains.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:40.989
At the time it was sunk, the original crew
of the Bismarck boasted a minimum of two thousand

00:02:40.989 --> 00:02:41.989
men.

00:02:41.989 --> 00:02:43.170
Where were their bodies?

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:47.109
Continuing the mission, the researchers piloted
their unmanned drone down the eerie winding

00:02:47.109 --> 00:02:48.590
corridors.

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:54.640
Along several of the inner corridors of the
submerged wreckage of SCP-4217, the crew find

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:59.989
large thick walls of what appear to be made
out of a rubber-like substance.

00:02:59.989 --> 00:03:04.420
Soon they find that the large vein-like growths
extend throughout the interior of the ship

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:09.819
like tendrils, growing in size the closer
the exploratory drone gets to the center of

00:03:09.819 --> 00:03:10.900
the vessel.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:15.719
All the while a slight hum sound is picked
up by the craft’s sonar equipment, echoing

00:03:15.719 --> 00:03:19.040
from the center of the ship, a rhythmic pulsing.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:23.290
The crew decide they need to take a sample
of the rubber-like substance back to Foundation

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:25.090
headquarters for testing.

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:27.310
This would be a mistake.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:31.069
Upon cutting into the thick tentacle-like
growths, the researchers notice something

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:33.569
that fills their stomachs with dread.

00:03:33.569 --> 00:03:37.629
Whatever substance they had cut into was now
bleeding.

00:03:37.629 --> 00:03:41.030
The team hears a distant rumble growing steadily
louder.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:44.189
Suddenly the ship begins to move!

00:03:44.189 --> 00:03:49.480
Shuffling sand and debris strew along the
seafloor, clouding the visibility of the ship.

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:53.529
Terrified - the pair hurry to try and disconnect
the cable attaching the probe to their submersible

00:03:53.529 --> 00:03:54.799
and evacuate the site.

00:03:54.799 --> 00:03:56.299
But it’s too late.

00:03:56.299 --> 00:04:00.790
A booming thud shakes the underwater craft
as a large shadow covers the glass window

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:02.099
of the submersible.

00:04:02.099 --> 00:04:05.799
Alarm systems go off as cracks start to appear
in the glass surface.

00:04:05.799 --> 00:04:09.879
The pair attempt to pilot the vessel up toward
the surface but they are halted by a strong

00:04:09.879 --> 00:04:12.019
force pulling them downward.

00:04:12.019 --> 00:04:16.410
Just as the cracks start to spread across
the surface of the glass, a giant shadow looms

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:17.870
over the submersible.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:20.150
“Wha-..what is that?!”

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:24.389
Screams and the sound of shattering glass
can be heard on the recording as the submersible

00:04:24.389 --> 00:04:27.720
implodes from the pressure of the watery depths.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:34.460
Since that unfortunate event, Foundation members
have recorded multiple occurances of SCP-4217

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:39.710
attacking civilian cargo ships in the Atlantic,
particularly off the coast of the United Kingdom

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:42.389
and as far north as the Greenland Sea.

00:04:42.389 --> 00:04:48.389
Given it’s Keter containment classification,
containment of SCP-4217 consists of constant

00:04:48.389 --> 00:04:53.800
monitoring by Foundation naval forces with
the cooperation of the British Royal Navy.

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:59.110
In episodes of aggression or an “agitated
or hostile state”, naval forces are instructed

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:04.240
to forcibly subdue SCP-4217 through naval
engagement.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:10.460
Once enough damage is sustained, SCP-4217
enters a “passive” state and re-submerges.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:15.520
SCP-4217 is divided into two parts.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:22.200
SCP-4217-A is the Bismarck itself - a Nazi-era
warship outfitted with an array of 8 main

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:29.870
guns, 44 secondary armaments, and a dozen
units of anti-aircraft weaponry.

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:38.129
SCP-4217-B refers to the “anomalous cephalopod
organism” embedded inside the hull of the

00:05:38.129 --> 00:05:39.129
ship.

00:05:39.129 --> 00:05:43.220
SCP-4217-B has two large rectangular pupils
inside of octopoid eyes that protrude from

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:49.669
the base of the ship, as well as twelve 100
to 200 meter-long tendril-like muscular appendages

00:05:49.669 --> 00:05:53.800
that extend outward from an opening in the
stern of the vessel.

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:59.160
SCP-4217 is deemed to be classification risk
class: Dangerous, with reports of it emitting

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:04.830
a mild psionic field within a 20 km radius,
confusing anything within range and increasing

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:08.789
the likelihood of friendly fire among enemy
combatants.

00:06:08.789 --> 00:06:15.069
SCP-4217-A’s hull seems to have the ability
of inorganic regeneration, as damage incurred

00:06:15.069 --> 00:06:19.610
from enemy vessels seem to immaculately repair
over time.

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:23.400
Researchers have observed what appear to be
runes or cryptic markings on the sides of

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:26.440
SCP-4217-A’s hull.

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:31.289
It is believed these symbols were part of
the original ship’s design to bolster the

00:06:31.289 --> 00:06:33.110
vessel’s defensive integrity.

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:38.120
Though not immediately visible, when the vessel
is taking fire, the symbols appear to glow

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:41.400
“in proportion to the amount of damage being
mitigated”.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:47.780
Among it’s offensive capabilities, apart
from the standard armaments of a WW2 era warship,

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:53.490
SCP-4217-A also has specialized munitions
of an unidentifiable gas compound that is

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:56.289
reported to have “mutagenic properties”.

00:06:56.289 --> 00:07:01.530
Individuals that have been exposed to the
gas compound undergo rapid spontaneous metamorphosis

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:06.070
at a molecular level, growing an array of
evolutionary attributes which include the

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:11.620
accumulation of reptile-like scales or avian
feathers in place of skin, the increase or

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:17.409
decrease of the number of limbs, digits, or
even ocular, olfactory, or auditory, organs,

00:07:17.409 --> 00:07:23.250
and in one reported case, an event where multiple
members of one crew were fused at a subatomic

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:29.060
level into one functioning organism, though
more study into this particular incident is

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:30.260
needed.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:35.759
SCP-4217 also has the ability of sub-surface
oceanic mobility, and can submerge itself

00:07:35.759 --> 00:07:38.629
when not in combat with enemy vessels.

00:07:38.629 --> 00:07:44.151
Underwater propulsion appears to be generated
by ejection of water from SCP-4217-B’s body

00:07:44.151 --> 00:07:49.370
cavity, and reaches a top speed of approximately
30 knots.

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:54.620
SCP-4217 undergoes cycles of passive behavior
that is periodically interrupted by moments

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:59.879
of hostility towards civilian craft, particularly
resurfacing and going after trans-atlantic

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:01.229
cargo vessels.

00:08:01.229 --> 00:08:06.360
It is believed this is analogous to the history
and original mission of the Bismarck, operation

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:07.990
Rheinubung.

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:12.400
During World War 2, the German Luftwaffe were
besieging London in a series of nightly air

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:15.680
raids that would be colloquially known as
the Blitz.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:20.389
It was the grand intention of the Third Reich
to cut off supplies to the British to limit

00:08:20.389 --> 00:08:22.780
their resistance to the Nazi war machine.

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:28.870
However what pestered the Nazis most and hindered
this effort was the consistant American support

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:33.650
provided by the U.S. government in the form
of food and supplies delivered to the British

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:36.210
via Atlantic trade routes by cargo ship.

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:40.650
The German Bismarck and her sister ship, the
Tirpitz, were created for the very goal of

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:45.160
stopping these transports of cargo to the
United Kingdom, as well as sinking as many

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:47.230
allied vessels as possible.

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:49.450
The year is 1937.

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:53.950
In a top secret effort to make preparations
for an approaching war, Adolf Hitler turns

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:59.590
to his most trusted expert on the supernatural,
chief SS officer Heinrich Himmler.

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:04.700
Among other projects, Himmler ordered the
Ahnenerbe Obskurakorps, a German organization

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:09.470
tasked with the procurement and investigation
of otherworldly or otherwise unexplainable

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:14.980
phenomenon, to begin the creation of two ships,
the Bismarck and the Tirpitz, the former named

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:20.540
after the Iron Chancellor, Otto Von Bismarck,
who in 1890 unified the German people.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:25.390
These vessels were to be created using recently
uncovered technological oddities the Obskurakorps

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:27.870
had found in their studies of the occult.

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:33.660
Sources of information about the exact creation
of SCP-4217 are highly expunged from the record.

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:38.320
But bits and pieces did survive among what
little the Foundation was able to collect

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:42.780
and in the records of the USSR after their
occupation of Eastern Germany following the

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:46.070
fall of the Nazi regime during the second
world war.

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:52.550
The earliest mention of SCP-4217’s conception
dates back to early 1937, when a top-secret

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:58.150
shipment of unknown materials labeled as “components
of thaumatological constructs” is intercepted

00:09:58.150 --> 00:10:03.530
by a Foundation agent working undercover in
a German shipment center outside of Hamburg.

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:08.540
The Foundation agent, Markus Straub, is instructed
to maintain surveillance on the shipment.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:13.421
In 1939, upon near completion of the soon
to be chirstianed “Bismarck”, a second

00:10:13.421 --> 00:10:17.730
shipment labeled with the insignia of the
Obskuracorps is intercepted by the Foundation

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:18.760
agent.

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:22.070
Only this shipment appears unlike any other.

00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:25.570
Reports of the massive shipping container
holding machinery capable of aquatic life

00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:28.690
support indicate organic living cargo.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:32.620
Though the Foundation agent was unable to
identify the exact nature of the contents

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:37.420
of the shipment, Straub reported hearing sounds
emanating from the cargo hold.

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:40.090
Sounds similar to that of a heartbeat.

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:45.200
Just a year later the Bismarck is seen making
its first naval trial run when it experiences

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:50.350
a massive electrical discharge just offshore,
shutting the vessel down momentarily until

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:52.870
power was restored shortly after.

00:10:52.870 --> 00:10:57.050
Reports show luminescent symbols briefly visible
on the hull of the ship.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:11:01.590
Thaumatological symbols, for the layman, are
symbols that embody the “study of miracles”.

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:06.160
Because of this, it was apparent to the Foundation
that some occult anomaly was responsible for

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:11.010
the strange characteristics of the German
vessel, and an order for termination was reached

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:12.640
by the O5 council.

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:16.060
The hunt for SCP-4217:

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:22.770
In the autumn of 1940, under orders of neutralization
of SCP-4217, all active Foundation agents

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:27.170
presiding in Germany were ordered to converge
on the site of the Bismark to stop the completion

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:28.170
of the vessel.

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:32.790
But when the time came for the operation,
every single one of the Foundation agents

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:33.850
vanished.

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:39.460
No records of what happened were ever found,
no clothing, notes, not even a trace of their

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:41.240
existence was left behind.

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:47.430
The mission was deemed a failure, and subsequent
attempts to neutralize SCP-4217 became far

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:50.890
more difficult after the Bismarck received
a full crew of seamen.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:57.040
The fully manned and well equipped SCP-4217
became a menace to both military and civilian

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:01.690
craft on the high seas of the Atlantic, at
times appearing without warning seemingly

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:03.580
out of thin air.

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:08.890
SCP-4217’s psionic field obscured it from
the new technological advancements in enemy

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:12.350
radar systems the U.S. government had in development.

00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:16.940
The ship became a shadow on the Atlantic,
a subject of ghost stories for anyone daring

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:20.050
to assist the British government with the
war effort.

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:25.930
Furthermore, SCP-4217 did not seem to be content
with the surrender of enemy vessels.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:31.041
Captured enemy ships were gassed, turning
the men into manufactured beasts, and then

00:12:31.041 --> 00:12:34.310
sinking the enemy vessels to the depths of
the Ocean.

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:38.830
Even submarines were no match, on one report
describing an attempt to elude the vessel

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:44.480
by diving below the surface, only to be entangled
by enormous squid-like appendages that dragged

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:48.940
the craft back up to the surface before crushing
it in its grasp.

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:52.680
Fearing for the safety of the public, the
O5 council decided they could not stand by

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:55.310
and let more innocent lives be taken.

00:12:55.310 --> 00:13:00.220
They voted to supersede the Foundation’s
policy on absolute secrecy to notify the British

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:05.440
government of the danger SCP-4217 posed to
maritime civilians.

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:09.580
With cooperation from the British Royal Navy,
Foundation representatives joined the crew

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:14.710
of HMS Hood and HMS Prince of Wales to track
reports of the Bismarck being sighted off

00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:16.380
the coast of Scandinavia.

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:21.020
In what history books would come to know as
the battle of the Denmark Strait, HMS Hood

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:28.750
and HMS Prince of Wales engage SCP-4217 and
a secondary German warship known as the Prinz

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:29.750
Eugen.

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:33.610
Confused by the ship’s psionic field, the
British naval ships experience trouble identifying

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:38.790
the Bismarck and engage in friendly fire before
being able to regain control of their armaments,

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:40.910
concentrating all volley of fire on SCP-4217.

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:48.140
The attack proves futile, as after the embers
and smoke of munitions fire wear off, the

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:52.270
sides of the Bismarck’s hull appear to vibrate
with glowing energy.

00:13:52.270 --> 00:13:57.100
Mangled metal begins to straighten back into
perfect frame, breaches in armor begin to

00:13:57.100 --> 00:14:01.840
heal before the soldier’s very eyes, and
all that is left as evidence the ship had

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:08.320
ever taken fire is a cloud of steam emanating
from the hull of SCP-4217.

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:12.180
The waters surrounding the vessel begin to
boil as underwater tentacles lurch out and

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:16.330
capture the HMS Hood, dragging her majesty’s
ship forward.

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:21.290
The men aboard frantically try to regain control,
but seconds later are met with another crisis.

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:27.830
A salvo of artillery shells fired from SCP-4217’s
guns hits the ship, severing lines and damaging

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:33.500
rail guns as a mutagenic gas compound starts
to spread among the Royal seamen.

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:37.951
In mere minutes, the majority of the crew
are engulfed in toxic fumes and experience

00:14:37.951 --> 00:14:43.890
vomiting and convulsions, their bodies undergoing
rapid involuntary mutagenesis including the

00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:48.070
growth of limbs, the development of fur, feathers
and scales.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:53.730
In one report, it was said that multiple victims
even fused together to create one single horrifying

00:14:53.730 --> 00:14:54.730
entity.

00:14:54.730 --> 00:15:00.360
Those exposed to the gaseous compound were
designated SCP-4217-1.

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:04.930
The captain of the HMS Hood barricades himself
inside the helm, but the resulting instances

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:09.420
of SCP-4217-1 overpower the ship and neutralize
command.

00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:13.820
In the seconds that follow, any witness of
the horror that the men aboard the HMS Hood

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:19.050
experienced is forever entombed in the watery
grave of the British vessel, as the ship is

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:23.950
sunk by a volley of munitions fire from the
combined might of the German fleet.

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:27.630
Some men attempting to jump overboard and
swim to safety are dragged down by their legs

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:34.690
by the mutated instances of SCP-4217 and pulled
under, lungs filling with sea water as they

00:15:34.690 --> 00:15:37.890
scream until their breath is no more.

00:15:37.890 --> 00:15:42.640
In disbelief, the crew of HMS Prince of Wales
decides to retreat.

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:47.060
In the days that followed, at the bequest
of Foundation members, the British Royal Navy

00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:51.610
launches a full scale armada to hunt down
and neutralize the Bismarck.

00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:57.250
Though SCP-4217 sustained little damage in
the previous encounter, the ship began leaking

00:15:57.250 --> 00:16:02.620
a black oil-like substance thought by SCP
researchers to be an organic waste product

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:05.510
of SCP-4217-B.

00:16:05.510 --> 00:16:09.601
The allied naval force are able to follow
the trail to the coast of France, where, under

00:16:09.601 --> 00:16:15.650
the lead of HMS King George V, British warships
surround the German vessel and open fire.

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:17.490
This time they were ready.

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:22.240
With approval from the O5 Council, Foundation
members provide the British forces with enhanced

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:28.710
munitions and armament capable of overwhelming
SCP-4217’s thaumatological defenses.

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:33.100
On the eve of battle, it appears to the allied
force that the psionic field generated by

00:16:33.100 --> 00:16:39.050
SCP-4217 is too great, as the naval company
find it difficult to land targeted assaults

00:16:39.050 --> 00:16:40.630
on the German vessel.

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:46.781
After losing several smaller vessels to the
colossal appendages of SCP-4217, Foundation

00:16:46.781 --> 00:16:50.530
members on board authorize the use of a redacted
SCP.

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:54.680
It is brought in to deactivate SCP-4217’s
psionic field.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.450
The tide of battle turns.

00:16:56.450 --> 00:17:02.660
And after a fierce battle, SCP-4217 becomes
imobile and unable to return fire.

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:07.600
Relentless, the British continue their bombardment
until the artillery munitions on the ship

00:17:07.600 --> 00:17:12.720
explode into a giant fireball, flooding the
ship’s compartments with the noxious fumes

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:14.299
of the mutagenic compound.

00:17:14.299 --> 00:17:18.880
It’s crew members either jump overboard
or are engulfed in the cloud of gas.

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:25.189
The British vessels capture any survivors
and watch as SCP-4217 slowly sinks below the

00:17:25.189 --> 00:17:31.830
waves, down to the depths of the ocean where
it would lay dormant for the next 48 years.

00:17:31.830 --> 00:17:37.169
SCP-4217’s 121 surviving crew members were
captured and interrogated.

00:17:37.169 --> 00:17:41.960
Most of the low-ranking German soldiers were
released to British custody, 109 of them having

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:44.480
their memory wiped by Foundation staff.

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:49.620
12 remaining members of the crew were sent
to Site-23 for further detention and advanced

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:57.380
interrogation, and 74 of the instances of
SCP-4217-1, the mutated subjects, were recovered

00:17:57.380 --> 00:18:00.210
and sent to Site-23 for further observation.

00:18:00.210 --> 00:18:06.770
It was thought that on that day SCP-4217 was
deemed neutralized and no longer a matter

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:07.880
of priority.

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:10.620
The Bismarck sunk into memory and myth.

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:16.350
It was only until the recent resurgence of
SCP-4217 that the Foundation saw the need

00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:22.879
to collect as much information on the organism
inhabiting SCP-4217-A as possible.

00:18:22.879 --> 00:18:27.450
Decades-old manuscripts and ledgers were pulled
from hundreds of viable sources.

00:18:27.450 --> 00:18:32.090
From the intelligence then gathered, Foundation
members have come to the hypothesis that the

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:37.370
entity powering the vessel known as the Bismarck
has what is believed to be extra-planetary

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:38.670
origin.

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:43.470
World War 2 era documents uncovered between
Commander Karl Reuter, of the German Obskuracorps,

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:49.299
and a Dr. Hans Meyer, indicate a discovery
of an organic life form of unknown origin

00:18:49.299 --> 00:18:54.480
found in a crashed aircraft near Feldberg
Peak in the Black Forest Mountain Range in

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:55.650
Germany.

00:18:55.650 --> 00:19:00.580
Further correspondence with Obskuracorps members
Otto Schmidt and Dietrich Klossner indicate

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:05.100
that researchers were conducting trials on
the creature’s ability to create pisonic

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:10.720
fields, and to control or confuse enemy subjects
within it’s range, with a letter from Dietrich

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:14.990
Klossner suggesting the creature could be
used as a power source for an unspecified

00:19:14.990 --> 00:19:16.330
“engine”.

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:23.850
Further evidence of SCP-4217-B’s extra-planetary
origin can be found in a 1993 incident between

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:29.559
Foundation naval ship SCPS Nemed and SCP-4217.

00:19:29.559 --> 00:19:33.879
This is the only incident on record where
contact was established with the creature

00:19:33.879 --> 00:19:41.929
classified as SCP-4217-B.
On July 22nd, SCP-4217 had reappeared off

00:19:41.929 --> 00:19:43.410
the coast of Britain.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:51.370
Anticipating hostility, SCPS Nemed, SCPS Cesair,
and SCPS Parthalon were instructed to close

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:57.049
in on SCP-4217’s location with orders to
subdue the vessel if necessary.

00:19:57.049 --> 00:20:03.399
However, on this occasion, SCP-4217 did not
appear to be after any vessel.

00:20:03.399 --> 00:20:08.309
It was simply drifting along at sea, no propulsion
engines active.

00:20:08.309 --> 00:20:14.590
Noticing the change in SCP-4217’s behavior,
captain Kurt Wegner decided to withhold military

00:20:14.590 --> 00:20:19.149
engagement and investigate SCP-4217’s behavior.

00:20:19.149 --> 00:20:24.289
Sailing within 200 meters of the Bismarck,
the SCPS Nemed attempted radio contact with

00:20:24.289 --> 00:20:25.760
the German vessel.

00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:30.610
After repeated attempts at communication,
the crew were met with only silence and static

00:20:30.610 --> 00:20:31.610
chatter.

00:20:31.610 --> 00:20:36.059
Giving up, Captain Wegner puts down the radio
receiver when suddenly, the sound of music

00:20:36.059 --> 00:20:38.161
is heard playing over the speakers of his
ship.

00:20:38.161 --> 00:20:42.490
The tune is the national anthem of Nazi Germany.

00:20:42.490 --> 00:20:46.030
The captain hails the vessel again, repeating
his attempts at communication.

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:49.190
“Do you..do you understand me?”

00:20:49.190 --> 00:20:55.779
At first only static can be heard, then came
a reply..

00:20:55.779 --> 00:21:00.299
“You..ship?” the ominous voice could be
heard from the speakers.

00:21:00.299 --> 00:21:05.120
The captain hesitated for a moment, members
of the crew looking at each other with apprehension.

00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:11.289
The captain replied, confirming themselves
as a ship and then asking if SCP-4217 knew

00:21:11.289 --> 00:21:13.830
what is was and where it came from.

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:20.350
What followed was the crew of the SCPS Nemed
receiving a video feed from SCP-4217 featuring

00:21:20.350 --> 00:21:23.700
a high volume of images in rapid succession.

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:29.110
Among them were images of German cities, Adolf
Hitler’s telecast of the 1936 Olympics,

00:21:29.110 --> 00:21:35.120
an unknown structure in outer space, and in
increasing repetition, images of the planet

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:41.280
Jupiter, particularly the giant storm on Jupiter
known to the public as the Great Red Spot,

00:21:41.280 --> 00:21:44.850
or SCP-2399 as foundation members know it.

00:21:44.850 --> 00:21:50.590
The transcript of the radio communication
between captain Wagner and SCP-2417 stops

00:21:50.590 --> 00:21:55.159
when the video feed begins to focus heavily
on images of Jupiter.

00:21:55.159 --> 00:22:01.410
SCP-4217’s responses become more erratic
and agitated as it repeats the words “Storm”,

00:22:01.410 --> 00:22:06.070
“Cloud”, and “Red”, the markings on
it’s hulls beginning to light up and the

00:22:06.070 --> 00:22:10.450
underwater shadows of it’s tentacles beginning
to create whirlpools of displacement under

00:22:10.450 --> 00:22:11.559
the bow of the ship.

00:22:11.559 --> 00:22:16.940
A shrill shrieking begins to flood out of
the speakers followed by a piercing high-pitched

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:22.840
beeping sound that overloads the communication
equipment causing sparks to fly as crew members

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:25.740
cover their ears and hide under control panels.

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:32.500
The SCPS Nemed barely escapes as SCP-4217
becomes hostile, using its massive tendril-like

00:22:32.500 --> 00:22:38.080
appendages to assail the naval combatants,
firing it’s armamnet in all directions.

00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:42.440
After a fierce battle, the Foundation naval
forces were able to neutralize and subdue

00:22:42.440 --> 00:22:44.830
SCP-4217.

00:22:44.830 --> 00:22:47.669
No further attempts at communication have
been recorded.

00:22:47.669 --> 00:22:52.450
To keep the veil of secrecy, Foundation members
constructed a replica ship to be sunk and

00:22:52.450 --> 00:22:58.149
intentionally re-discovered by oceanographer
Robert Ballard in 1989.

00:22:58.149 --> 00:23:03.809
Any recent sightings of the Nazi-era Bismarck
are flagged as misidentifications by SCP staff.

00:23:03.809 --> 00:23:10.690
For now, Foundation members continue to monitor
the behavior of SCP-4217 and protect the public

00:23:10.690 --> 00:23:12.490
from its existence.

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:19.870
Now go check out “SCP-1861 - The Crew of
the HMS Wintersheimer” and “SCP-5987 - Sirenhead”

00:23:19.870 --> 00:23:23.950
for more anomalous underwater vessels from
SCP Explained!

